From 9c935ea9306343f77712f6489fd0c2187f241718 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 13:42:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] fix: eliminate enum import and member access issues in
 detection generation pipeline

- Convert DetectionFormat and RuleSeverity from type-only to value imports across all generators
- Update default severity from string literals to enum members (RuleSeverity.HIGH)
- Fix lib/api/detection-rules.ts to use enum members for format array defaults
- Fix lib/detection/generators/siem.ts, sigma.ts, suricata.ts severity defaults
- Fix lib/detection/generators/yara.ts severity score record with computed property names
- Fix lib/detection/validators.ts format property values using enum members
- Explicitly type suricataRules and semRules variables to fix implicit any[] errors
- Remove type-only import of DetectionFormat from validators

Reduces TypeScript errors from 271 to 167 (104 total eliminated).
Eliminates cascading errors throughout detection rule generation pipeline.
Maintains strict TypeScript typing without weakening type safety.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PcqZQMLx2zqEEPRtdAX17K
